  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a half marathon and kept adding kilometres. A tiny sore spot on the shin showed up late in runs, then earlier, then on walks.\n\nBone is always repairing itself. When training load outpaces that repair, a bone stress injury can build. Pain you can cover with a fingertip that keeps progressing is a common clue.\n\nThings that often help: not running through focal, worsening pain, building volume gradually, eating enough for your training, and cross-training while it heals, followed by strength work and a graded return to running.\n\nPain at rest or at night, or pain in the groin, hip or top of the foot, should be assessed promptly. See your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
